diff --git a/host/camera_linux/README.md b/host/camera_linux/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9a33eaaf4ac7ad5b077e621203e8c96075a44505
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/camera_linux/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,137 @@
+# Z19 Linux camera 0 bench
+
+This directory ports the already demonstrated FL0214/IMX214 camera-0 sequence
+to Linux. It does not configure hand actuators. The unchanged hardware inputs,
+reviewed bit/XSA and provenance are archived in
+[camera_hw](../../fpga/camera_hw/README.md); external originals remain preserved.
+
+The bench profile is tied to the previously tested four-camera XSA bitstream:
+
+- bit SHA256: `28e1e3e7963ff12f57848998cf2695dcca139c3f519c5f020daf90dec4dc35ae`
+- Bootgen raw bin SHA256: `e25e9bc7fd4c2008c7a198a91bc4937716b333259d08da7ed777d8ffe9b3384b`
+- camera 0 VDMA: `0xA0060000`, scalar Digilent gamma: `0xA0040000`, reset GPIO: `0xA0080000`
+- PS I2C0, `/dev/i2c-0`, sensor `0x10`, lens actuator `0x0c`
+- PL clocks approximately 200/100 MHz; PS HP1 interface is 128 bits
+- Linux `5.4.0-xilinx-v2020.2`, AArch64, GCC 9.2.0
+- 1920×1080, BGR DMA bytes inferred from supplied RTL/XSA remap; three owned buffers (page-aligned stride 6221824)
+
+The XSA has conflicting derived `C_NUM_FSTORES=6` and actual configurable
+`c_num_fstores=3` values. The tested bit cycles indices 0/1/2. All six address
+pairs are filled with aliases of allocated memory defensively; consumers use
+only the three observed stores. Do not extrapolate this to another bitstream.
+
+`sensor_table.h` preserves all 89 register/value entries from the tested
+bare-metal `live_v2/src`; only trailing whitespace/newlines were normalized.
+Original SHA256 `e4875d6bf8bec230e173ee97706837ea20d3d6a955f386069a39e48a509a2a5b`;
+repository header SHA256 `136cffb7aedb45659e86a7abb5b5bcd2c772012e8177268d9348dbc857623ebf`.
+The CSI source holds FIFO reset for 200 million byte-clock cycles and delays
+writes for another 100 million. Capture waits up to 30 seconds for real frame
+transitions, then begins measurement. A 500 ms delay was insufficient at first.
+
+## Build on the board
+
+The shipped kernel header tree lacks host tools and generated ARM wrappers.
+Build an isolated copy, preserving `/lib/modules/.../build`:
+
+```sh
+export PATH=/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
+# Use a new, nonexistent destination; never overwrite an existing build tree.
+cp -a /lib/modules/$(uname -r)/build /var/lib/amazinghand/build/kernel-camera-20261010
+K=/var/lib/amazinghand/build/kernel-camera-20261010
+make -C "$K" ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE= HOSTCC=gcc scripts
+make -C "$K" ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE= HOSTCC=gcc asm-generic
+make -C "$K" ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE= HOSTCC=gcc prepare0
+cd /path/to/copied/camera_linux
+make KERNEL_DIR="$K" module
+make capture
+```
+
+Native syncconfig adds only `CONFIG_CC_CAN_LINK` and updates the compiler label;
+it does not change the running kernel. The rebuilt module was actually loaded
+and used to capture frames; vermagic alone is not the validation.
+
+Convert a copy of the reviewed XSA's `design_1_wrapper.bit` with the existing
+Bootgen, using a BIF containing `[destination_device=pl] camera.bit`:
+
+```text
+bootgen -image camera.bif -arch zynqmp -process_bitstream bin
+```
+
+Verify both hashes above, transfer the raw bin into `/lib/firmware`, then run
+the guarded manual loader. It checks hashes, module ABI, active PL users,
+clocks and the relevant PS interface registers before programming.
+
+```sh
+sh /opt/amazinghand/bin/load_z19_camera0.sh \
+  /lib/firmware/amazinghand-camera-28e1e3e7-20261010.bin ./ah_camera0.ko
+./capture_camera0 10 /var/lib/amazinghand/log/NEW_CAPTURE.raw 300
+python3 test_device.py idle
+python3 start_preview.py
+```
+
+On the directly connected PC, run `python host/camera_linux/view_camera.py`
+and open `http://127.0.0.1:8766/`. This loopback viewer forwards only camera
+HTTP routes directly to the board, preserving the PC's existing proxy settings.
+Stop it with Ctrl+C. The board service remains available at
+`http://192.28.14.153:9000/` when the browser can connect directly.
+
+Preview now uses a persistent **1920×1080 MJPEG stream**, with no upscaling
+from the old 320×180 image. A 30-second PC receive test decoded all 757 JPEGs
+at 1920×1080, measured 25.161 frames/s, and found 757 different frames with
+no missing published sequences. This measures received frames, not browser
+rendering or lossless sensor acquisition. Actual rate depends on scene and
+clients; the page displays the measured publishing rate and supports fullscreen.
+Earlier 5 Hz snapshots and 320×180/29.4 Hz streaming are retained as history
+in the bring-up log, not the current resolution.
+Focus 0–1023 is a manual actuator position, not autofocus. No detection model
+or robot-control process runs in this UI.
+The helper detaches the server from SSH and prints a PID/log path; SIGTERM to
+that verified PID stops the server. The capture also checks parent-process
+liveness and stops if its server disappears. It is not an automatic boot service.
+Four copy slices move the complete coherent DMA frame into ordinary RAM;
+two native libjpeg-turbo workers encode BGR directly at quality 85. The board
+already provides libjpeg-turbo 2.0.3 and development headers; no new packages
+were installed. The Python server forwards encoded JPEGs without re-encoding.
+Validate optical color against a known target; haze/focus is not resolved by
+increasing resolution.
+
+Copies begin just after a buffer transition. The complete status/copy/status
+window must be at most 30 ms and the selected store must remain non-writable.
+This bound is specific to the reviewed sensor profile, observed at ~55.6 Hz:
+a complete overwrite and wrap requires at least two periods (~36 ms).
+Do not reuse this bound for faster sensor modes. No mapping/cache properties
+or driver ABI changed. Busy/unsafe/obsolete copies are discarded and counted;
+JPEG workers only read cached copies. Metadata cannot regress in capture time.
+Clients receive the newest published sequence without an application backlog.
+A stale/error/stop closes an existing stream and rejects new frame requests.
+
+Current deployment: `/opt/amazinghand/camera0-linux-hd-20261010`.
+The old package is preserved. To run fault tests without overwriting prior
+evidence, provide `python3 test_preview.py --output /path/to/NEW_RESULT.json`.
+On the PC, `test_stream.py --seconds 30 --output NEW.json --snapshot NEW.jpg`
+checks every received JPEG's resolution, sequence, capture time and delivery
+intervals. It uses PC Pillow; do not install that dependency onto the board.
+A separate 60-second HD run published 1666 frames without copy/busy/obsolete
+discards, stopped DMA normally, joined workers and saved a 6220800-byte raw.
+The service uses a one-hour capture session; press Start again after it ends.
+
+Chinese operating steps: [`camera_quickstart.md`](../../docs/fpga/camera_quickstart.md).
+
+## Ownership and shutdown
+
+- One open owner; unknown ioctls, writable/partial/private/offset mappings are rejected.
+- DMA buffers use `dma_alloc_coherent` and `dma_mmap_coherent`, limited below 4 GiB.
+- File/VMA references prevent unloading the module while buffers are mapped.
+- Normal stop: sensor stream off → VDMA halted → save stable previous store → unmap → close.
+- Last file release, including process death, resets CSI and halts/resets VDMA.
+- If hardware cannot halt, memory is retained, new opens are refused, and a
+  critical message requires power-cycle recovery. It is never returned for reuse
+  while DMA may still access it.
+- Never reprogram PL with this module loaded. Stop the owned capture, check
+  that the device is no longer open/mapped, then `rmmod ah_camera0` first.
+- SD BOOT.BIN/FIT are unchanged. A reboot loads the old baseline PL; manually
+  load this reviewed camera profile again before capturing. Automatic boot and
+  camera cold-start reliability are separate pending acceptance items.
+
+Actual board results and limitations are recorded in
+[`docs/fpga/linux_camera0_bringup.md`](../../docs/fpga/linux_camera0_bringup.md).
diff --git a/host/camera_linux/ah_camera0.c b/host/camera_linux/ah_camera0.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b4593b8976d925cc804d99da86d768b0799093a0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/camera_linux/ah_camera0.c
@@ -0,0 +1,220 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/* Camera-0 bench driver for bit SHA256 28e1e3e7963ff12f57848998cf2695dcca139c3f519c5f020daf90dec4dc35ae.
+ * DMA allocation follows the supplied ALINX mipi_cam.c. This driver owns VDMA
+ * start/stop and maps coherent buffers through the DMA API, not /dev/mem.
+ * Load only after checking firmware hash, clocks, HP1 width and idle PL users.
+ * No automatic boot loading. No hand-control registers are accessed.
+ */
+#include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/miscdevice.h>
+#include <linux/fs.h>
+#include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
+#include <linux/of_device.h>
+#include <linux/mm.h>
+#include <linux/io.h>
+#include <linux/iopoll.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/uaccess.h>
+#include <linux/mutex.h>
+#include "ah_camera0_uapi.h"
+
+#define WIDTH 1920U
+#define HEIGHT 1080U
+#define FRAME_BYTES (WIDTH * HEIGHT * 3U)
+#define BUFFERS 3U
+#define VDMA_BASE 0xa0060000UL
+#define GPIO_BASE 0xa0080000UL
+#define CR 0x30
+#define SR 0x34
+#define ERROR_BITS 0xff0U
+
+static bool matched_pl;
+module_param(matched_pl, bool, 0400);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(matched_pl, "Explicit acknowledgement of verified camera PL profile");
+static void __iomem *vdma, *gpio;
+static void *frames;
+static dma_addr_t dma_base;
+static size_t stride, map_bytes;
+static u64 dma_mask = DMA_BIT_MASK(32);
+static bool opened;
+static DEFINE_MUTEX(camera_lock);
+
+/* Reset CSI/sensor first on close, then halt/reset VDMA. Never free active DMA. */
+static int stop_dma(void)
+{
+	u32 value;
+	writel(0, gpio);
+	writel(readl(vdma + CR) & ~1U, vdma + CR);
+	if (!readl_poll_timeout(vdma + SR, value, value & 1, 100, 200000))
+		return 0;
+	writel(4, vdma + CR);
+	if (readl_poll_timeout(vdma + CR, value, !(value & 4), 100, 200000))
+		return -ETIMEDOUT;
+	return readl_poll_timeout(vdma + SR, value, value & 1, 100, 200000);
+}
+
+static int camera_open(struct inode *inode, struct file *file)
+{
+	int ret = 0;
+	mutex_lock(&camera_lock);
+	if (opened)
+		ret = -EBUSY;
+	else
+		opened = true;
+	mutex_unlock(&camera_lock);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static int camera_release(struct inode *inode, struct file *file)
+{
+	int ret;
+	mutex_lock(&camera_lock);
+	ret = stop_dma();
+	if (ret)
+		pr_crit("ah_camera0: DMA failed to halt; buffers remain allocated\n");
+	else
+		opened = false;
+	mutex_unlock(&camera_lock);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static long camera_ioctl(struct file *file, unsigned int cmd, unsigned long arg)
+{
+	struct ah_camera0_info info = {0};
+	struct ah_camera0_status status;
+	u32 value;
+	int ret = 0, i;
+	mutex_lock(&camera_lock);
+	switch (cmd) {
+	case AH_CAM_INFO:
+		for (i = 0; i < BUFFERS; i++)
+			info.dma_addr[i] = dma_base + i * stride;
+		info.frame_bytes = FRAME_BYTES;
+		info.buffer_stride = stride;
+		info.map_bytes = map_bytes;
+		info.width = WIDTH;
+		info.height = HEIGHT;
+		info.buffers = BUFFERS;
+		info.abi_version = 1;
+		ret = copy_to_user((void __user *)arg, &info, sizeof(info)) ? -EFAULT : 0;
+		break;
+	case AH_CAM_START:
+		if (!(readl(vdma + SR) & 1)) { ret = -EBUSY; break; }
+		writel(4, vdma + CR);
+		ret = readl_poll_timeout(vdma + CR, value, !(value & 4), 100, 200000);
+		if (ret) break;
+		memset(frames, 0, map_bytes);
+		writel(0xfff0, vdma + SR);
+		writel(0, vdma + 0x44);
+		/* Raw configurable c_num_fstores=3; derived C_NUM_FSTORES=6 is stale.
+		 * Fill all six address pairs with owned memory as a defensive measure. */
+		for (i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
+			u64 addr = dma_base + (i % BUFFERS) * stride;
+			writel(lower_32_bits(addr), vdma + 0xac + i * 8);
+			writel(upper_32_bits(addr), vdma + 0xb0 + i * 8);
+		}
+		writel(WIDTH * 3, vdma + 0xa4);
+		writel(WIDTH * 3, vdma + 0xa8);
+		/* Continuous circular mode, stream TUSER SOF, no IRQ enable. */
+		writel(0x00010043, vdma + CR);
+		writel(HEIGHT, vdma + 0xa0);
+		break;
+	case AH_CAM_STOP:
+		ret = stop_dma();
+		break;
+	case AH_CAM_STATUS:
+		status.control = readl(vdma + CR);
+		status.status = readl(vdma + SR);
+		status.write_index = (readl(vdma + 0x28) >> 24) & 31;
+		status.version = readl(vdma + 0x2c);
+		ret = copy_to_user((void __user *)arg, &status, sizeof(status)) ? -EFAULT : 0;
+		break;
+	case AH_CAM_CLEAR:
+		writel(0xfff0, vdma + SR);
+		break;
+	default:
+		ret = -ENOTTY;
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&camera_lock);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static int camera_mmap(struct file *file, struct vm_area_struct *vma)
+{
+	if (vma->vm_pgoff || vma->vm_end - vma->vm_start != map_bytes ||
+	    vma->vm_flags & VM_WRITE || !(vma->vm_flags & VM_MAYSHARE))
+		return -EINVAL;
+	vma->vm_flags &= ~VM_MAYWRITE;
+	vma->vm_flags |= VM_DONTEXPAND | VM_DONTDUMP;
+	return dma_mmap_coherent(file->private_data ?
+		((struct miscdevice *)file->private_data)->this_device : NULL,
+		vma, frames, dma_base, map_bytes);
+}
+
+static const struct file_operations camera_fops = {
+	.owner = THIS_MODULE,
+	.open = camera_open,
+	.release = camera_release,
+	.unlocked_ioctl = camera_ioctl,
+	.mmap = camera_mmap,
+	.llseek = no_llseek,
+};
+
+static struct miscdevice camera_misc = {
+	.minor = MISC_DYNAMIC_MINOR,
+	.name = "ah_camera0",
+	.fops = &camera_fops,
+	.mode = 0600,
+};
+
+static int __init camera_init(void)
+{
+	struct device *dev;
+	int ret;
+	if (!matched_pl) return -EPERM;
+	vdma = ioremap(VDMA_BASE, 4096);
+	gpio = ioremap(GPIO_BASE, 4096);
+	if (!vdma || !gpio) { ret = -ENOMEM; goto unmap; }
+	if (readl(vdma + 0x2c) != 0x62000050) { ret = -ENODEV; goto unmap; }
+	ret = stop_dma();
+	if (ret) goto unmap;
+	ret = misc_register(&camera_misc);
+	if (ret) goto unmap;
+	dev = camera_misc.this_device;
+	dev->dma_mask = &dma_mask;
+	ret = of_dma_configure(dev, NULL, true);
+	if (ret) goto deregister;
+	ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+	if (ret) goto deregister;
+	stride = PAGE_ALIGN(FRAME_BYTES);
+	map_bytes = stride * BUFFERS;
+	frames = dma_alloc_coherent(dev, map_bytes, &dma_base, GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!frames) { ret = -ENOMEM; goto deregister; }
+	memset(frames, 0, map_bytes);
+	pr_info("ah_camera0: %u x %u RGB, %u buffers, DMA=0x%llx map=%zu\n",
+		WIDTH, HEIGHT, BUFFERS, (unsigned long long)dma_base, map_bytes);
+	return 0;
+deregister:
+	misc_deregister(&camera_misc);
+unmap:
+	if (gpio) iounmap(gpio);
+	if (vdma) iounmap(vdma);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static void __exit camera_exit(void)
+{
+	if (stop_dma())
+		pr_crit("ah_camera0: refusing to free unhalted DMA memory; power cycle required\n");
+	else
+		dma_free_coherent(camera_misc.this_device, map_bytes, frames, dma_base);
+	misc_deregister(&camera_misc);
+	iounmap(gpio);
+	iounmap(vdma);
+}
+
+module_init(camera_init);
+module_exit(camera_exit);
+MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
+MODULE_DESCRIPTION("AmazingHand reviewed Z19 camera-0 bench capture");
+MODULE_AUTHOR("AmazingHand; allocation reference ALINX mipi_cam.c");
diff --git a/host/camera_linux/ah_camera0_uapi.h b/host/camera_linux/ah_camera0_uapi.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d3423eff406f42849e7dbc3347ee177cdb9db97d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/camera_linux/ah_camera0_uapi.h
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+/* Fixed-width bench ABI; this device supports only the reviewed camera-0 PL. */
+#ifndef AH_CAMERA0_UAPI_H
+#define AH_CAMERA0_UAPI_H
+#include <linux/types.h>
+#include <linux/ioctl.h>
+
+struct ah_camera0_info {
+	__u64 dma_addr[3];
+	__u32 frame_bytes;
+	__u32 buffer_stride;
+	__u32 map_bytes;
+	__u32 width;
+	__u32 height;
+	__u32 buffers;
+	__u32 abi_version;
+	__u32 reserved;
+};
+
+struct ah_camera0_status {
+	__u32 control;
+	__u32 status;
+	__u32 write_index;
+	__u32 version;
+};
+
+#define AH_CAM_INFO _IOR('A', 1, struct ah_camera0_info)
+#define AH_CAM_START _IO('A', 2)
+#define AH_CAM_STOP _IO('A', 3)
+#define AH_CAM_STATUS _IOR('A', 4, struct ah_camera0_status)
+#define AH_CAM_CLEAR _IO('A', 5)
+#endif
diff --git a/host/camera_linux/camera_preview.c b/host/camera_linux/camera_preview.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..12c57bbd9a70afe182478d924fd731b9a111255d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/camera_linux/camera_preview.c
@@ -0,0 +1,221 @@
+/* Copy completed coherent DMA stores into ordinary RAM before encoding.
+ * Four disjoint copy slices reduce noncached-read latency. Two JPEG workers
+ * overlap encoding with capture; busy/unsafe/obsolete frames are discarded.
+ * JPEG workers never access DMA, MMIO or I2C. No DMA cache attributes change.
+ */
+#define _POSIX_C_SOURCE 200809L
+#include <errno.h>
+#include <fcntl.h>
+#include <pthread.h>
+#include <setjmp.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <sys/ioctl.h>
+#include <time.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+#include <jpeglib.h>
+#include "camera_preview.h"
+
+#define WIDTH 1920U
+#define HEIGHT 1080U
+#define BYTES (WIDTH * HEIGHT * 3U)
+#define WORKERS 2U
+
+struct jpeg_errors { struct jpeg_error_mgr base; jmp_buf jump; };
+struct job {
+    pthread_t thread;
+    uint8_t *pixels, *jpeg;
+    unsigned long jpeg_bytes;
+    unsigned capture;
+    double stamp, copy_ms;
+    int state; /* 0 free, 1 copying, 2 ready, 3 encoding */
+    struct jpeg_compress_struct codec;
+    struct jpeg_errors errors;
+};
+static struct job jobs[WORKERS];
+static pthread_mutex_t lock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
+static pthread_cond_t ready = PTHREAD_COND_INITIALIZER;
+static unsigned created, published, capture_sequence, last_capture;
+static unsigned busy_skips, copy_discards, obsolete_discards;
+static int stopping, failed;
+static char directory[4096];
+
+static double now(void) {
+    struct timespec t;
+    clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &t);
+    return t.tv_sec + t.tv_nsec / 1e9;
+}
+static void jpeg_error(j_common_ptr codec) {
+    struct jpeg_errors *errors = (struct jpeg_errors *)codec->err;
+    (*codec->err->output_message)(codec);
+    longjmp(errors->jump, 1);
+}
+static int encode(struct job *job) {
+    memset(&job->codec, 0, sizeof(job->codec));
+    job->jpeg = NULL;
+    job->jpeg_bytes = 0;
+    job->codec.err = jpeg_std_error(&job->errors.base);
+    job->errors.base.error_exit = jpeg_error;
+    if (setjmp(job->errors.jump)) {
+        jpeg_destroy_compress(&job->codec);
+        free(job->jpeg);
+        job->jpeg = NULL;
+        return -1;
+    }
+    jpeg_create_compress(&job->codec);
+    jpeg_mem_dest(&job->codec, &job->jpeg, &job->jpeg_bytes);
+    job->codec.image_width = WIDTH;
+    job->codec.image_height = HEIGHT;
+    job->codec.input_components = 3;
+    job->codec.in_color_space = JCS_EXT_BGR;
+    jpeg_set_defaults(&job->codec);
+    jpeg_set_quality(&job->codec, 85, TRUE);
+    job->codec.dct_method = JDCT_FASTEST;
+    jpeg_start_compress(&job->codec, TRUE);
+    while (job->codec.next_scanline < HEIGHT) {
+        JSAMPROW row = job->pixels + job->codec.next_scanline * WIDTH * 3;
+        if (jpeg_write_scanlines(&job->codec, &row, 1) != 1) {
+            jpeg_destroy_compress(&job->codec);
+            free(job->jpeg);
+            job->jpeg = NULL;
+            return -1;
+        }
+    }
+    jpeg_finish_compress(&job->codec);
+    jpeg_destroy_compress(&job->codec);
+    return 0;
+}
+/* Called with lock held: serialize metadata publication, never regress time. */
+static int publish(struct job *job, double encode_ms) {
+    char path[4096], meta[4096], temp[4096], name[64];
+    unsigned next = published + 1;
+    if (job->capture <= last_capture) { obsolete_discards++; return 0; }
+    snprintf(name, sizeof(name), "preview-%08u.jpg", next);
+    if (snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%s/%s", directory, name) >= (int)sizeof(path) ||
+        snprintf(meta, sizeof(meta), "%s/metadata.json", directory) >= (int)sizeof(meta) ||
+        snprintf(temp, sizeof(temp), "%s/metadata.json.next", directory) >= (int)sizeof(temp)) return -1;
+    int fd = open(path, O_WRONLY | O_CREAT | O_EXCL, 0600);
+    if (fd < 0) return -1;
+    size_t written = 0;
+    while (written < job->jpeg_bytes) {
+        ssize_t result = write(fd, job->jpeg + written, job->jpeg_bytes - written);
+        if (result < 0 && errno == EINTR) continue;
+        if (result <= 0) { close(fd); return -1; }
+        written += result;
+    }
+    if (close(fd)) return -1;
+    FILE *output = fopen(temp, "wx");
+    if (!output) return -1;
+    int error = fprintf(output,
+        "{\"sequence\":%u,\"capture_sequence\":%u,\"file\":\"%s\",\"monotonic\":%.6f,"
+        "\"published_monotonic\":%.6f,\"capture_width\":1920,\"capture_height\":1080,"
+        "\"preview_width\":1920,\"preview_height\":1080,\"copy_ms\":%.3f,\"encode_ms\":%.3f,"
+        "\"copy_discards\":%u,\"busy_skips\":%u,\"obsolete_discards\":%u}\n",
+        next, job->capture, name, job->stamp, now(), job->copy_ms, encode_ms,
+        copy_discards, busy_skips, obsolete_discards) < 0;
+    if (fclose(output)) error = 1;
+    if (error || rename(temp, meta)) return -1;
+    published = next;
+    last_capture = job->capture;
+    if (next > 8) {
+        if (snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%s/preview-%08u.jpg", directory, next - 8) >= (int)sizeof(path)) return -1;
+        if (unlink(path)) return -1;
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+static void *encoder(void *arg) {
+    struct job *job = arg;
+    for (;;) {
+        pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);
+        while (!stopping && job->state != 2) pthread_cond_wait(&ready, &lock);
+        if (stopping) { pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock); break; }
+        job->state = 3;
+        pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
+        double begin = now();
+        int error = encode(job);
+        double encode_ms = (now() - begin) * 1000;
+        pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);
+        if (error || (!stopping && publish(job, encode_ms))) failed = 1;
+        free(job->jpeg);
+        job->jpeg = NULL;
+        job->state = 0;
+        pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
+    }
+    return NULL;
+}
+struct slice { uint8_t *dst; const uint8_t *src; size_t bytes; };
+static void *copy_slice(void *arg) {
+    const struct slice *slice = arg;
+    memcpy(slice->dst, slice->src, slice->bytes);
+    return NULL;
+}
+static int initialize(const char *dir) {
+    if (snprintf(directory, sizeof(directory), "%s", dir) >= (int)sizeof(directory)) return -1;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < WORKERS; i++) {
+        if (posix_memalign((void **)&jobs[i].pixels, 64, BYTES)) return -1;
+        if (pthread_create(&jobs[i].thread, NULL, encoder, &jobs[i])) return -1;
+        created++;
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+int camera_preview(const char *dir, int fd, const uint8_t *frames,
+                   const struct ah_camera0_info *info, unsigned *sequence) {
+    struct ah_camera0_status before, after;
+    if (!created && initialize(dir)) return -1;
+    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);
+    *sequence = published;
+    if (failed) { pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock); return -1; }
+    struct job *job = NULL;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < WORKERS; i++) if (!jobs[i].state) { job = &jobs[i]; break; }
+    if (!job) { busy_skips++; pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock); return 0; }
+    job->state = 1;
+    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
+    double begin = now();
+    if (ioctl(fd, AH_CAM_STATUS, &before) || before.write_index >= 3 || before.status & 0xff1) return -1;
+    unsigned done = (before.write_index + 2) % 3;
+    const uint8_t *source = frames + done * info->buffer_stride;
+    pthread_t threads[4];
+    struct slice slices[4];
+    unsigned started = 0;
+    __sync_synchronize();
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+        slices[i] = (struct slice){job->pixels + i * (BYTES / 4), source + i * (BYTES / 4), BYTES / 4};
+        if (pthread_create(&threads[i], NULL, copy_slice, &slices[i])) break;
+        started++;
+    }
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < started; i++) pthread_join(threads[i], NULL);
+    __sync_synchronize();
+    if (started != 4 || ioctl(fd, AH_CAM_STATUS, &after)) return -1;
+    /* Include both status queries in the bound, so a delayed final ioctl
+     * cannot hide a complete write and wrap of the selected store. */
+    job->copy_ms = (now() - begin) * 1000;
+    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);
+    /* This fixed sensor profile runs at ~55.6 Hz (18 ms/store). A complete
+     * overwrite-and-wrap of the previous completed store needs at least two
+     * periods (~36 ms). Bound the entire status/copy/status window to 30 ms
+     * and reject if that store became writable. Do not reuse for faster modes. */
+    if (job->copy_ms > 30 || after.write_index == done || after.status & 0xff1) {
+        copy_discards++;
+        job->state = 0;
+    } else {
+        job->capture = ++capture_sequence;
+        job->stamp = now();
+        job->state = 2;
+        pthread_cond_broadcast(&ready);
+    }
+    *sequence = published;
+    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
+    return 0;
+}
+void camera_preview_shutdown(void) {
+    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);
+    stopping = 1;
+    pthread_cond_broadcast(&ready);
+    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < created; i++) pthread_join(jobs[i].thread, NULL);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < WORKERS; i++) free(jobs[i].pixels);
+    printf("PREVIEW_HD published=%u copy_discards=%u busy_skips=%u obsolete_discards=%u\n",
+           published, copy_discards, busy_skips, obsolete_discards);
+}
diff --git a/host/camera_linux/camera_preview.h b/host/camera_linux/camera_preview.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d5086f48ae68a052d5f736b80dd6567deb09cb3d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/camera_linux/camera_preview.h
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+#ifndef CAMERA_PREVIEW_H
+#define CAMERA_PREVIEW_H
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include "ah_camera0_uapi.h"
+int camera_preview(const char *dir, int fd, const uint8_t *frames,
+                   const struct ah_camera0_info *info, unsigned *sequence);
+void camera_preview_shutdown(void);
+#endif
diff --git a/host/camera_linux/capture_camera0.c b/host/camera_linux/capture_camera0.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f9e49c5672733e43a82a12860e85a2980399308e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/camera_linux/capture_camera0.c
@@ -0,0 +1,243 @@
+/* Linux port of the already validated Z19 CAM0 bare-metal sequence.
+ * Usage: capture_camera0 SECONDS OUTPUT.raw [FOCUS_POSITION [NEW_PREVIEW_DIR]]
+ * A normal exit stops sensor/VDMA before saving and unmapping. Existing output
+ * is never overwritten. The supplied register table must be copied alongside.
+ */
+#define _POSIX_C_SOURCE 200809L
+#include <errno.h>
+#include <fcntl.h>
+#include <inttypes.h>
+#include <linux/i2c.h>
+#include <linux/i2c-dev.h>
+#include <signal.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <sys/ioctl.h>
+#include <sys/mman.h>
+#include <sys/stat.h>
+#include <time.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+#include "ah_camera0_uapi.h"
+#include "sensor_table.h"
+#include "camera_preview.h"
+
+static volatile sig_atomic_t quitting;
+static void on_signal(int sig) { (void)sig; quitting = 1; }
+static double now(void) {
+    struct timespec ts;
+    clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts);
+    return ts.tv_sec + ts.tv_nsec / 1e9;
+}
+static void delay_ms(unsigned ms) {
+    struct timespec ts = { ms / 1000, (ms % 1000) * 1000000L };
+    while (nanosleep(&ts, &ts) && errno == EINTR && !quitting) {}
+}
+static int transfer(int fd, struct i2c_msg *msgs, unsigned count) {
+    struct i2c_rdwr_ioctl_data data = { .msgs = msgs, .nmsgs = count };
+    int ret = ioctl(fd, I2C_RDWR, &data);
+    if (ret != (int)count) { perror("I2C_RDWR"); return -1; }
+    return 0;
+}
+static int sensor_write(int fd, unsigned reg, unsigned value) {
+    uint8_t bytes[3] = { reg >> 8, reg & 255, value };
+    struct i2c_msg msg = { .addr = 0x10, .len = 3, .buf = bytes };
+    int ret = transfer(fd, &msg, 1);
+    delay_ms(1);
+    return ret;
+}
+static int sensor_read(int fd, unsigned reg, uint8_t *value) {
+    uint8_t addr[2] = { reg >> 8, reg & 255 };
+    struct i2c_msg msgs[2] = {
+        { .addr = 0x10, .len = 2, .buf = addr },
+        { .addr = 0x10, .flags = I2C_M_RD, .len = 1, .buf = value }
+    };
+    return transfer(fd, msgs, 2);
+}
+static int set_focus(int fd, unsigned position) {
+    uint8_t bytes[2] = { position >> 4, (position & 15) << 4 };
+    struct i2c_msg msg = { .addr = 0x0c, .len = 2, .buf = bytes };
+    return transfer(fd, &msg, 1);
+}
+static uint32_t sample_hash(const uint8_t *frame, unsigned bytes, unsigned *nonzero) {
+    uint32_t value = 2166136261U;
+    *nonzero = 0;
+    for (unsigned p = 0; p < bytes; p += 5009) {
+        value = (value ^ frame[p]) * 16777619U;
+        *nonzero += frame[p] != 0;
+    }
+    return value;
+}
+static int write_frame(const char *path, const uint8_t *frame, unsigned bytes) {
+    int fd = open(path, O_WRONLY | O_CREAT | O_EXCL, 0600);
+    if (fd < 0) { perror("create raw frame"); return -1; }
+    unsigned written = 0;
+    while (written < bytes) {
+        ssize_t result = write(fd, frame + written, bytes - written);
+        if (result < 0 && errno == EINTR) continue;
+        if (result <= 0) { perror("write raw frame"); close(fd); return -1; }
+        written += result;
+    }
+    int ret = fsync(fd);
+    if (close(fd) && !ret) ret = -1;
+    return ret;
+}
+int main(int argc, char **argv) {
+    struct ah_camera0_info info = {0};
+    struct ah_camera0_status status = {0};
+    int camera = -1, i2c = -1, mem = -1, ret = 1, started = 0, valid = 0;
+    uint8_t *frames = MAP_FAILED;
+    volatile uint32_t *gpio = MAP_FAILED, *gamma = MAP_FAILED;
+    unsigned seconds, focus = 300, changes = 0, last_changes = 0, seen = 0, preview_sequence = 0;
+    uint8_t hi, lo, wh, wl, hh, hl;
+    char *end;
+    if (argc < 3 || argc > 5) { fprintf(stderr, "usage: %s SECONDS NEW_OUTPUT.raw [FOCUS_0_1023 [NEW_PREVIEW_DIR]]\n", argv[0]); return 2; }
+    unsigned long duration = strtoul(argv[1], &end, 10);
+    if (!*argv[1] || *end || duration < 1 || duration > 3600) return 2;
+    seconds = duration;
+    if (argc >= 4) {
+        unsigned long position = strtoul(argv[3], &end, 10);
+        if (!*argv[3] || *end || position > 1023) return 2;
+        focus = position;
+    }
+    if (access(argv[2], F_OK) == 0) { fprintf(stderr, "output exists; refusing overwrite\n"); return 2; }
+    if (argc == 5 && mkdir(argv[4], 0700)) { perror("new preview directory"); return 2; }
+    setvbuf(stdout, NULL, _IOLBF, 0);
+    signal(SIGINT, on_signal);
+    signal(SIGTERM, on_signal);
+    pid_t parent = getppid();
+    camera = open("/dev/ah_camera0", O_RDONLY | O_CLOEXEC);
+    if (camera < 0) { perror("open camera"); goto done; }
+    if (ioctl(camera, AH_CAM_INFO, &info)) { perror("buffer info"); goto done; }
+    if (info.abi_version != 1 || info.width != 1920 || info.height != 1080 ||
+        info.buffers != 3 || info.frame_bytes != 6220800 ||
+        info.buffer_stride < info.frame_bytes || info.map_bytes != info.buffer_stride * 3) goto done;
+    frames = mmap(NULL, info.map_bytes, PROT_READ, MAP_SHARED, camera, 0);
+    if (frames == MAP_FAILED) { perror("map DMA buffers"); goto done; }
+    printf("BUFFERS 0x%" PRIx64 " 0x%" PRIx64 " 0x%" PRIx64 " stride=%u bytes=%u\n",
+           (uint64_t)info.dma_addr[0], (uint64_t)info.dma_addr[1], (uint64_t)info.dma_addr[2], info.buffer_stride, info.map_bytes);
+    mem = open("/dev/mem", O_RDWR | O_SYNC | O_CLOEXEC);
+    if (mem < 0) { perror("open registers"); goto done; }
+    gpio = mmap(NULL, 4096, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_SHARED, mem, 0xa0080000);
+    gamma = mmap(NULL, 4096, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_SHARED, mem, 0xa0040000);
+    if (gpio == MAP_FAILED || gamma == MAP_FAILED) { perror("map registers"); goto done; }
+    gpio[1] = 0; gpio[0] = 0; delay_ms(20); gpio[0] = 3; delay_ms(20);
+    i2c = open("/dev/i2c-0", O_RDWR | O_CLOEXEC);
+    if (i2c < 0) { perror("open I2C0"); goto done; }
+    if (sensor_read(i2c, 0x16, &hi) || sensor_read(i2c, 0x17, &lo)) goto done;
+    printf("CAM0_SENSOR_ID 0x%02x%02x\n", hi, lo);
+    if (hi != 2 || lo != 0x14 || sensor_write(i2c, 0x100, 0)) goto done;
+    delay_ms(20);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; sensor_init_data[i].reg != SEQUENCE_END; i++) {
+        unsigned reg = sensor_init_data[i].reg, val = sensor_init_data[i].val;
+        if (quitting || getppid() != parent) goto done;
+        if (reg == SEQUENCE_WAIT_MS) { delay_ms(val); continue; }
+        if (reg == 0x100) continue; /* Start only after owned DMA is configured. */
+        if (sensor_write(i2c, reg, val)) { fprintf(stderr, "register 0x%04x failed\n", reg); goto done; }
+    }
+    gamma[0] = 3; /* Reviewed Digilent scalar gamma IP, not legacy LUT registers. */
+    if (set_focus(i2c, focus)) goto done;
+    printf("FOCUS_POSITION %u (manual)\n", focus);
+    if (sensor_read(i2c, 0x34c, &wh) || sensor_read(i2c, 0x34d, &wl) ||
+        sensor_read(i2c, 0x34e, &hh) || sensor_read(i2c, 0x34f, &hl)) goto done;
+    printf("SENSOR_DIMENSIONS %ux%u\n", (wh << 8) | wl, (hh << 8) | hl);
+    if (((wh << 8) | wl) != 1920 || ((hh << 8) | hl) != 1080) goto done;
+    if (ioctl(camera, AH_CAM_START)) { perror("start DMA"); goto done; }
+    started = 1;
+    if (sensor_write(i2c, 0x100, 1)) goto done;
+    delay_ms(500);
+    uint8_t stream, count1, count2;
+    if (sensor_read(i2c, 0x100, &stream) || sensor_read(i2c, 5, &count1)) goto done;
+    delay_ms(100);
+    if (sensor_read(i2c, 5, &count2)) goto done;
+    printf("SENSOR_STREAM %u COUNTER %u -> %u\n", stream, count1, count2);
+    /* The supplied CSI RTL holds FIFO reset for 200M byte-clock cycles,
+     * then gates writes for another 100M. Wait for actual frames, not a
+     * guessed 500ms delay; the initial byte clock exists only while streaming. */
+    double warmup_at = now();
+    unsigned warmup_index = 0, warmup_changes = 0;
+    while (!quitting && getppid() == parent && now() - warmup_at < 30) {
+        if (ioctl(camera, AH_CAM_STATUS, &status)) goto done;
+        if (status.write_index >= 3 || status.status & 1) goto done;
+        if (status.status & 0xff0) {
+            printf("WARMUP_DMA_STATUS 0x%08x\n", status.status);
+            if (ioctl(camera, AH_CAM_CLEAR)) goto done;
+        }
+        if (status.write_index != warmup_index) {
+            warmup_index = status.write_index; warmup_changes++;
+            if (warmup_changes >= 4) break;
+        }
+        delay_ms(10);
+    }
+    printf("WARMUP seconds=%.3f transitions=%u\n", now() - warmup_at, warmup_changes);
+    if (quitting || getppid() != parent || warmup_changes < 4) { fprintf(stderr, "CSI_STARTUP_TIMEOUT\n"); goto done; }
+    if (ioctl(camera, AH_CAM_CLEAR) || ioctl(camera, AH_CAM_STATUS, &status)) goto done;
+    unsigned previous = status.write_index;
+    double begin = now(), changed_at = begin, report_at = begin, preview_at = begin, published_at = begin;
+    printf("CAPTURE_STARTED seconds=%u\n", seconds);
+    while (!quitting && getppid() == parent && now() - begin < seconds) {
+        if (ioctl(camera, AH_CAM_STATUS, &status)) goto done;
+        if (status.status & 0xff0 || status.write_index >= 3 || status.status & 1) {
+            fprintf(stderr, "DMA_FAILURE status=0x%08x index=%u\n", status.status, status.write_index); goto done;
+        }
+        seen |= 1U << status.write_index;
+        int frame_changed = status.write_index != previous;
+        if (frame_changed) { changes++; changed_at = now(); previous = status.write_index; }
+        if (now() - changed_at > 2) { fprintf(stderr, "FRAME_STALLED\n"); goto done; }
+        /* Begin just after a store transition, giving a complete two-store
+         * window for the copy. Unsynchronized polling wastes safe frames. */
+        if (argc == 5 && frame_changed && now() - preview_at >= 1.0 / 30.0) {
+            preview_at = now();
+            unsigned old_sequence = preview_sequence;
+            if (camera_preview(argv[4], camera, frames, &info, &preview_sequence)) {
+                fprintf(stderr, "PREVIEW_PUBLISH_FAILED\n"); goto done;
+            }
+            if (preview_sequence != old_sequence) published_at = now();
+            if (now() - published_at > 5) { fprintf(stderr, "PREVIEW_STALLED\n"); goto done; }
+        }
+        if (now() - report_at >= 1) {
+            unsigned nonzero, done_index = (status.write_index + 2) % 3;
+            uint32_t hash = sample_hash(frames + done_index * info.buffer_stride, info.frame_bytes, &nonzero);
+            printf("{\"seconds\":%.3f,\"observed_transitions\":%u,\"interval_transitions\":%u,\"write_index\":%u,\"seen_mask\":%u,\"status\":%u,\"sample_hash\":%u,\"nonzero_samples\":%u}\n",
+                   now() - begin, changes, changes - last_changes, status.write_index, seen, status.status, hash, nonzero);
+            if (!nonzero) {
+                for (unsigned b = 0; b < 3; b++) {
+                    unsigned nz; uint32_t bh = sample_hash(frames + b * info.buffer_stride, info.frame_bytes, &nz);
+                    fprintf(stderr, "BUFFER%u hash=%u nonzero=%u\n", b, bh, nz);
+                }
+                fprintf(stderr, "EMPTY_FRAME\n"); goto done;
+            }
+            last_changes = changes;
+            report_at = now();
+        }
+        delay_ms(1);
+    }
+    if (quitting || getppid() != parent) { fprintf(stderr, "CAPTURE_INTERRUPTED\n"); goto done; }
+    if (changes < seconds * 5 || seen != 7) { fprintf(stderr, "INSUFFICIENT_FRAME_TRANSITIONS\n"); goto done; }
+    valid = 1;
+done:
+    if (i2c >= 0 && sensor_write(i2c, 0x100, 0)) { fprintf(stderr, "STREAM_OFF_FAILED\n"); valid = 0; }
+    if (camera >= 0) {
+        if (ioctl(camera, AH_CAM_STOP)) { perror("stop DMA"); valid = 0; }
+        else {
+            printf("DMA_HALTED\n");
+            if (started && valid && !ioctl(camera, AH_CAM_STATUS, &status) && status.write_index < 3) {
+                unsigned done_index = (status.write_index + 2) % 3, nonzero;
+                const uint8_t *frame = frames + done_index * info.buffer_stride;
+                sample_hash(frame, info.frame_bytes, &nonzero);
+                if (nonzero && !write_frame(argv[2], frame, info.frame_bytes)) {
+                    printf("CAPTURE_COMPLETE transitions=%u seen_mask=%u bytes=%u saved=%s\n", changes, seen, info.frame_bytes, argv[2]); ret = 0;
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    camera_preview_shutdown();
+    if (frames != MAP_FAILED) munmap(frames, info.map_bytes);
+    if (gamma != MAP_FAILED) munmap((void *)gamma, 4096);
+    if (gpio != MAP_FAILED) munmap((void *)gpio, 4096);
+    if (mem >= 0) close(mem);
+    if (i2c >= 0) close(i2c);
+    if (camera >= 0) close(camera);
+    return ret;
+}
diff --git a/host/camera_linux/preview_server.py b/host/camera_linux/preview_server.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f8916d037b56aec9af79d5cef614033335d61505
--- /dev/null
+++ b/host/camera_linux/preview_server.py
@@ -0,0 +1,267 @@
+"""Small Linux camera bench UI; serves genuine frames and explicit stale/errors.
+
+Uses the board's existing Python 3.7. Capture runs independently and
+publishes immutable full-resolution JPEGs in RAM. This is a camera preview, with no inference or
+hand-control actions. SIGTERM/exit stops the owned capture process.
+"""
+import argparse
+import ctypes
+import datetime
+import fcntl
+from http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer
+import json
+import os
+from pathlib import Path
+import re
+import signal
+import subprocess
+import threading
+import time
+
+HTML = '''<!doctype html><html lang="zh-CN"><meta charset="utf-8">
+<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
+<title>Z19 相机实时预览</title><style>
+body{font:16px system-ui;background:#101722;color:#e7eef8;margin:0;padding:24px}
+main{max-width:1440px;margin:auto}h1{font-size:24px}img{width:100%;background:#080d15;border-radius:12px;object-fit:contain}img:fullscreen{height:100vh;width:100vw;border-radius:0}
+button,input{font:inherit}button{padding:9px 18px;margin:6px;border:0;border-radius:8px;cursor:pointer}
+#state{font-weight:700;color:#f8ca70}#detail{color:#b2c2d7}section{padding:16px 0}
+</style><main><h1>Z19 相机实时预览</h1><p id="state">正在连接…</p>
+<p id="detail">1080p 高清实时视频 · 正在连接</p><img id="image" alt="等待相机画面" hidden>
+<section><button onclick="action('start')">启动</button><button onclick="action('stop')">停止</button>
+<button onclick="document.getElementById('image').requestFullscreen()">全屏</button>
+<p>手动焦距 <input id="focus" type="range" min="0" max="1023" value="300" oninput="document.getElementById('label').textContent=this.value">
+<span id="label">300</span><button onclick="action('focus',{position:Number(document.getElementById('focus').value)})">应用</button></p>
+<p id="message"></p></section></main><script>
+const image=document.getElementById('image'),state=document.getElementById('state'),detail=document.getElementById('detail');
+let streaming=false,busy=false;
+async function action(name,data={}){try{let r=await fetch('/'+name,{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify(data)});let j=await r.json();document.getElementById('message').textContent=j.message||'';}catch(e){document.getElementById('message').textContent='连接失败';}}
+async function update(){if(busy)return;busy=true;try{let r=await fetch('/status.json',{cache:'no-store'});let j=await r.json();state.textContent=j.message;state.style.color=j.state==='LIVE'?'#79e5b2':'#f8ca70';if(j.state==='LIVE'){detail.textContent='1080p 高清视频 · '+j.preview_width+'×'+j.preview_height+' · '+(j.preview_fps||0).toFixed(1)+' 帧/秒 · 最新帧 '+Math.round(j.age_seconds*1000)+' ms 前';if(!streaming){image.src='/stream.mjpg?t='+Date.now();streaming=true;}image.hidden=false;}else{image.hidden=true;streaming=false;image.removeAttribute('src');detail.textContent='1080p 高清视频 · 等待画面';}}catch(e){state.textContent='连接中断';image.hidden=true;streaming=false;image.removeAttribute('src');}finally{busy=false;}}
+image.onerror=()=>{image.hidden=true;streaming=false};setInterval(update,500);update();
+</script></html>'''
+
+
+class Camera:
+    def __init__(self, executable, log_dir, ram_dir):
+        self.executable = executable
+        self.log_dir = log_dir
+        self.ram_dir = ram_dir
+        self.proc = None
+        self.log = None
+        self.preview_dir = None
+        self.focus = 300
+        self.counter = 0
+        self.cache_sequence = None
+        self.jpeg = None
+        self.lock = threading.RLock()
+        self.rate_sample = None
+        self.preview_fps = 0.0
+
+    def start(self):
+        with self.lock:
+            if self.proc is not None and self.proc.poll() is None:
+                return '相机已在运行'
+            if self.log is not None:
+                self.log.close()
+            self.counter += 1
+            name = 'camera0-preview-' + datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y%m%d-%H%M%S') + '-%d' % self.counter
+            self.preview_dir = self.ram_dir / name
+            self.log = (self.log_dir / (name + '.txt')).open('xb')
+            raw = self.log_dir / (name + '.raw')
+            self.cache_sequence = None
+            self.rate_sample = None
+            self.preview_fps = 0.0
+            self.proc = subprocess.Popen([str(self.executable), '3600', str(raw), str(self.focus), str(self.preview_dir)],
+                                         stdout=self.log, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, close_fds=True)
+            return '相机正在启动，请等待画面'
+
+    def stop(self):
+        with self.lock:
+            if self.proc is not None and self.proc.poll() is None:
+                self.proc.terminate()
+                try:
+                    self.proc.wait(timeout=3)
+                except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
+                    self.proc.kill()
+                    self.proc.wait(timeout=3)
+            self.proc = None
+            self.jpeg = None
+            if self.log is not None:
+                self.log.close()
+                self.log = None
+            return '相机已停止'
+
+    def apply_focus(self, position):
+        if isinstance(position, bool) or not isinstance(position, int) or not 0 <= position <= 1023:
+            raise ValueError('焦距必须是 0～1023 的整数')
+        with self.lock:
+            if self.proc is None or self.proc.poll() is not None:
+                self.focus = position
+                return '下次启动将应用焦距 %d' % position
+
+            class Msg(ctypes.Structure):
+                _fields_ = [('addr', ctypes.c_ushort), ('flags', ctypes.c_ushort),
+                            ('length', ctypes.c_ushort), ('buf', ctypes.POINTER(ctypes.c_ubyte))]
+
+            class Transfer(ctypes.Structure):
+                _fields_ = [('msgs', ctypes.POINTER(Msg)), ('nmsgs', ctypes.c_uint)]
+
+            data = (ctypes.c_ubyte * 2)(position >> 4, (position & 15) << 4)
+            messages = (Msg * 1)(Msg(0x0c, 0, 2, data))
+            command = Transfer(messages, 1)
+            fd = os.open('/dev/i2c-0', os.O_RDWR)
+            try:
+                payload = bytearray(ctypes.string_at(ctypes.addressof(command), ctypes.sizeof(command)))
+                result = fcntl.ioctl(fd, 0x0707, payload, True)
+                if result != 1:
+                    raise RuntimeError('镜头调整失败')
+            finally:
+                os.close(fd)
+            self.focus = position
+            return '已应用手动焦距 %d' % position
+
+    def snapshot(self, image=False):
+        with self.lock:
+            result = {'state': 'STOPPED', 'message': '相机已停止', 'focus': self.focus}
+            if self.proc is None:
+                return result, None
+            code = self.proc.poll()
+            if code is not None:
+                result.update(state='ERROR' if code else 'STOPPED',
+                              message='采集异常，请检查连接后重新启动' if code else '相机已停止')
+                return result, None
+            try:
+                meta = json.loads((self.preview_dir / 'metadata.json').read_text())
+                if not re.fullmatch(r'preview-[0-9]{8}\.jpg', meta['file']):
+                    raise ValueError('unexpected frame name')
+                if (meta['preview_width'], meta['preview_height']) != (1920, 1080):
+                    raise ValueError('unexpected resolution')
+                age = time.monotonic() - meta['monotonic']
+                if age < 0 or age > .8:
+                    result.update(state='STALE', message='画面已停止更新', age_seconds=age)
+                    return result, None
+                if image and self.cache_sequence != meta['sequence']:
+                    encoded = (self.preview_dir / meta['file']).read_bytes()
+                    if not encoded.startswith(b'\xff\xd8') or not encoded.endswith(b'\xff\xd9'):
+                        raise ValueError('invalid JPEG')
+                    self.jpeg = encoded
+                    self.cache_sequence = meta['sequence']
+                stamp = meta['monotonic']
+                if self.rate_sample is None:
+                    self.rate_sample = (stamp, meta['sequence'])
+                elif stamp - self.rate_sample[0] >= 1:
+                    self.preview_fps = (meta['sequence'] - self.rate_sample[1]) / (stamp - self.rate_sample[0])
+                    self.rate_sample = (stamp, meta['sequence'])
+                result.update(state='LIVE', message='实时画面', age_seconds=age, sequence=meta['sequence'],
+                              preview_fps=self.preview_fps, capture_monotonic=stamp,
+                              preview_width=meta['preview_width'], preview_height=meta['preview_height'],
+                              copy_ms=meta['copy_ms'], encode_ms=meta['encode_ms'],
+                              copy_discards=meta['copy_discards'], busy_skips=meta['busy_skips'],
+                              obsolete_discards=meta['obsolete_discards'])
+                return result, self.jpeg if image else None
+            except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError):
+                result.update(state='STARTING', message='正在等待相机画面')
+                return result, None
+
+
+def main():
+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()
+    parser.add_argument('--capture', type=Path, default=Path(__file__).with_name('capture_camera0'))
+    parser.add_argument('--bind', default='192.28.14.153')
+    parser.add_argument('--port', type=int, default=9000)
+    parser.add_argument('--log-dir', type=Path, default=Path('/var/lib/amazinghand/log'))
+    parser.add_argument('--ram-dir', type=Path, default=Path('/run/amazinghand-preview'))
+    args = parser.parse_args()
+    if not args.capture.is_file():
+        raise RuntimeError('capture executable missing')
+    args.ram_dir.mkdir(mode=0o700, parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    camera = Camera(args.capture, args.log_dir, args.ram_dir)
+
+    class Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):
+        def reply(self, code, body, mime='application/json; charset=utf-8'):
+            self.send_response(code)
+            self.send_header('Content-Type', mime)
+            self.send_header('Content-Length', str(len(body)))
+            self.send_header('Cache-Control', 'no-store')
+            self.end_headers()
+            try:
+                self.wfile.write(body)
+            except (BrokenPipeError, ConnectionResetError):
+                pass
+
+        def do_GET(self):
+            path = self.path.split('?', 1)[0]
+            if path == '/':
+                self.reply(200, HTML.encode(), 'text/html; charset=utf-8')
+            elif path == '/status.json':
+                self.reply(200, json.dumps(camera.snapshot()[0], ensure_ascii=False).encode())
+            elif path == '/frame.jpg':
+                result, jpeg = camera.snapshot(image=True)
+                if result['state'] != 'LIVE' or jpeg is None:
+                    self.reply(503, b'{"error":"no fresh frame"}')
+                else:
+                    self.reply(200, jpeg, 'image/jpeg')
+            elif path == '/stream.mjpg':
+                result, jpeg = camera.snapshot(image=True)
+                if result['state'] != 'LIVE' or jpeg is None:
+                    self.reply(503, b'{"error":"no fresh frame"}')
+                    return
+                self.send_response(200)
+                self.send_header('Content-Type', 'multipart/x-mixed-replace; boundary=frame')
+                self.send_header('Cache-Control', 'no-store')
+                self.end_headers()
+                self.connection.settimeout(3)
+                last = None
+                try:
+                    while True:
+                        result, jpeg = camera.snapshot(image=True)
+                        if result['state'] != 'LIVE' or jpeg is None:
+                            break
+                        if result['sequence'] != last:
+                            header = ('--frame\r\nContent-Type: image/jpeg\r\nContent-Length: %d\r\n'
+                                      'X-Sequence: %d\r\nX-Capture-Monotonic: %.6f\r\n\r\n' %
+                                      (len(jpeg), result['sequence'], result['capture_monotonic'])).encode()
+                            self.wfile.write(header + jpeg + b'\r\n')
+                            self.wfile.flush()
+                            last = result['sequence']
+                        time.sleep(.003)
+                except (BrokenPipeError, ConnectionResetError, TimeoutError, OSError):
+                    pass
+            else:
+                self.reply(404, b'{}')
+
+        def do_POST(self):
+            try:
+                size = int(self.headers.get('Content-Length', '0'))
+                if size < 0 or size > 1024:
+                    raise ValueError('invalid request')
+                data = json.loads(self.rfile.read(size) or b'{}')
+                if self.path == '/start': message = camera.start()
+                elif self.path == '/stop': message = camera.stop()
+                elif self.path == '/focus': message = camera.apply_focus(data.get('position'))
+                else: self.reply(404, b'{}'); return
+                self.reply(200, json.dumps({'message': message}, ensure_ascii=False).encode())
+            except (ValueError, AttributeError, OSError, RuntimeError) as error:
+                self.reply(400, json.dumps({'message': str(error)}, ensure_ascii=False).encode())
+
+        def log_message(self, fmt, *values):
+            pass  # Frame requests do not flood persistent logs.
+
+    server = ThreadingHTTPServer((args.bind, args.port), Handler)
+    # Raise in the main thread so finally always stops the capture.
+    def terminate(sig, frame):
+        raise KeyboardInterrupt
+    signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, terminate)
+    signal.signal(signal.SIGHUP, terminate)
+    try:
+        print(camera.start(), flush=True)
+        print('PREVIEW_URL http://%s:%d/' % (args.bind, args.port), flush=True)
+        server.serve_forever(poll_interval=.2)
+    except KeyboardInterrupt:
+        pass
+    finally:
+        camera.stop()
+        server.server_close()
+
+
+if __name__ == '__main__':
+    main()
